<title>USA: Boston Technology added to S&amp;P Smallcap 600.</title>
<headline>Boston Technology added to S&amp;P Smallcap 600.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Equity Services Group of Standard &amp; Poor's said it would replace Mark Twain Bancshares in the S&amp;P SmallCap 600 Index with Boston Technology after the close of trading on April 25.</p>
<p>Mark Twain Bancshares is being acquired by Mercantile Bancorp in a friendly stock merger due to close on that date, S&amp;P said.</p>
<p>Boston Technology develops, makes and markets hardware and software products which provide enhanced voice, facsimile and information processing services.</p>
<p>((New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
</text>
